    {
      "rule_id": "MW-001",
      "fault_family": "mechanical_wear",
      "description": "Worn piston rings / oil consumption: oil slips past rings into combustion chamber, elevating HC. At higher RPM ring flutter improves sealing and HC drops \u2014 the opposite pattern of lean_condition where HC rises with RPM. Chemistry-primary rule: WORN_PISTON_RINGS as GATING evidence. v1 ERR-MW-003 reactivated with the shrtft1 IN_RANGE [-10,10] constraint removed \u2014 oil burning can foul O2 sensors, making trim-based constraints unreliable for ring-wear detection. OBD: hc > 200 ppm DEFINITIVE \u2014 ring-wear HC elevation exceeds the misfire hc>200 SUGGESTIVE, giving MW a structural advantage on high-HC cases (FT-10)",
      "chemistry_evidence": [
        {
          "state": "WORN_PISTON_RINGS",
          "tier": "GATING",
          "wiki_ref": "GAS_VOCABULARY \u00a73"
        }
