    {
      "rule_id": "MW-004",
      "fault_family": "mechanical_wear",
      "description": "Low compression / worn engine (general wear): cylinder sealing failure from worn rings, scored bores, or burned valves produces WORN_ENGINE chemistry \u2014 severely depressed CO2 (<12%) from incomplete combustion. OBD: map_kpa < 30.0 kPa as SUGGESTIVE (low intake vacuum at idle from weak cylinders unable to pull a strong vacuum stroke). v1 ERR-MW-006 expanded with MAP evidence (v1 had no OBD constraints). INCOMPLETE_COMBUSTION is DEFINITIVE \u2014 mechanical_wear is the primary consumer of this chemistry; misfire has no INCOMPLETE_COMBUSTION rule (FT-10 differentiation). MW-005 competes",
      "chemistry_evidence": [
        {
